### Query - Get All Reminders
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "query": "query { getReminders { success notifications { id title content schedule_type schedule_time last_sent is_active sender { id first_name last_name } recipients { status sent_at read_at } } errors { field message } } }"
}

### Query - Get Specific Reminder
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "query": "query($id: Int!) { getReminderById(id: $id) { success notifications { id title content schedule_type schedule_time last_sent is_active sender { id first_name last_name } recipients { status sent_at read_at } } errors { field message } } }",
  "variables": {
    "id": 1
  }
}

### Mutation - Cancel Reminder
POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "query": "mutation($notificationId: Int!) { cancelReminder(notificationId: $notificationId) }",
  "variables": {
    "notificationId": 1
  }
}

### Expected Responses:

# 1. Create Reminder Response:
# {
#   "data": {
#     "createReminder": true
#   }
# }

# 2. Get Reminders Response:
# {
#   "data": {
#     "getReminders": {
#       "success": true,
#       "notifications": [
#         {
#           "id": 1,
#           "title": "Daily Workout Reminder",
#           "content": "Time for your daily exercise!",
#           "schedule_type": "DAILY",
#           "schedule_time": "2024-01-20T14:30:00.000Z",
#           "last_sent": null,
#           "is_active": true,
#           "sender": {
#             "id": 1,
#             "first_name": "John",
#             "last_name": "Doe"
#           },
#           "recipients": [
#             {
#               "status": "PENDING",
#               "sent_at": null,
#               "read_at": null
#             }
#           ]
#         }
#       ],
#       "errors": null
#     }
#   }
# }

# 3. Cancel Reminder Response:
# {
#   "data": {
#     "cancelReminder": true
#   }
# }

### Testing Steps:
# 1. First create a reminder using one of the create mutations
# 2. Copy the returned reminder ID
# 3. Use that ID to test the getReminderById query
# 4. Test canceling the reminder using the same ID
# 5. Verify the reminder is no longer active using getReminders query

### Notes:
# - All times should be in UTC (ISO 8601 format)
# - schedule_type must be one of: "ONCE", "DAILY", "WEEKLY", "MONTHLY"
# - The reminder will be sent at the specified time in the user's timezone
# - For recurring reminders (DAILY, WEEKLY, MONTHLY), the schedule_time sets the initial time and recurrence pattern
# - Canceled reminders will still appear in queries but with is_active = false


